The BubbleTools are a set of printer drivers which convert G3-Fax,
PBM and PPM-color files into printable data. Printers which should
work with these tools are:

        Cannon Bubble Jet printers (tested on BJC-70).
        IBM Proprinter X24E (tested on BJC70 in emulation mode)
        Epson LQ1550 (tested on BJC70 in emulation mode)
        Epson Stylus (bug: line feeds need to be fixed, but read on)

and compatibles.

I have written the programs with the Canon BJC-70 which claims to emulate
either an IBM Proprinter X24E or an Epson LQ1550. The programs run fine there.
On other printers, your mileage may vary...

