mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.os.linux.announce

   I'm announcing here LPR2 v1.2e.

   LPR2 is a utility to select the pages you print from a postscript
document. It's orginially intended and mostly used to print recto/verso
(duplex) documents on recto only (simplex) printers, by printing every
other page on a stack of paper, then feeding the output back to the printer
to print on the other side of the sheets.

   Version 1.2e added a more usable interface to page selection, increased
the comments (it could be said that the file is a text file annotated by
a program rather than a commented program ;).

   A LSM description is included below.

   Help save the world's forests and save half the space taken by printed
documents by non-duplex printers: use lpr2 ! Also note that other postscript
utilities exist, that can help save paper, like the mpage utility, or the
psutil package (tell me if there's more); they have much more features than
poor LPR2, when they do work, but I found them to work reliably with very few
of the postscript documents I've tried them with, while LPR2 works perfectly 
for all of them. Find these utilities on your standard ftp sites or ask archie!

   I uploaded the file on the sunsite.unc.edu:pub/Linux/ in Incoming/
(to be in system/Printing/ I think, but always check the INDEX.whole file !)
Please tell me where else to upload/announce this program !
   It's also available from my WWW page, whose address is
"http://www.eleves.ens.fr:8080/home/rideau".

   Any feedback welcome !

