I've uploaded skim version 0.6 to sunsite. You can find it in:

    sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/Incoming/skim-0.6.tgz

but it will soon move to:

    sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/system/News/readers/skim-0.6.tgz

What is skim?
-------------
Skim is a graphical offline newsreader for Linux, which is designed to
minimize the online time when using a slow modem line (for example, 14K4
Slip or PPP).

Skim is useful when your phone company or Internet access provider charges 
for online time, or when conventional newsreaders are too slow.      

What's new in version 0.6?
--------------------------
* skim supports regular expressions to automatically select and kill subjects. 

* xskim allows you to use your favorite editor to edit new articles and
  replies, instead of the limited builtin editor.

* The user interface is streamlined. Skimming articles in xskim can now be 
  done with one mouse click per article, instead of three.

* Skim builds it's index files much faster when performing 'skim articles'
  and 'skim indexes'.

* When skim retrieves articles, it no longer creates a session with the news 
  server when no articles are selected in a group.

* Fixed some installation problems and a discrepancy between skim and xskim.

