I am happy to announce Linux Omen Reader (LORE) version 0.65.
This is it's first public release.

I   What is OMEN
================
  OMEN (Off-line Message Environment)  is off-line format like QWK. Omen is
  much more flexible than  QWK and it hasn't QWK's stupid  limit of  size
  of subject.

II What is LORE
===============
  LORE is  omen-reader - full featured  off-line  reader.  LORE  uses ANSI
  compatible  color terminal  (looks very good)  or VT-100  compatible B/W
  terminal.

  LORE  has  pull  down menus  and keyboard-commands for  advanced use. It
  has automatic  compiling/installation script, and it  has setup-dialogs,
  so user don't have to edit configuration files manually.

  Before  you  compile  LORE you can make changes to lore.h. These  include 
  colors of different objects and limits of messages/skip lists. This allow
  bigger message packets than OMEN standard...

  Lore is licensed under GNU General Public License version 2.

III Miscellaneous
=================
  If you need some feature, just contact author, and I will add it to next 
  release of LORE (if I have time and interest to do that).

  Also all bug reports/bug fixes/port wishes are welcome.


