-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

The Linux Activists mailing lists at niksula.hut.fi will be closed
August 11th 1995.

We think that the current state of the lists is unacceptable because
  - the list handler software is hard to use and breaks about once a
    month, causing everyone a lot of annoyance
  - we receive hundreds of error replies a day because of bad
    destination addresses
  - nobody has been really administering the lists for some time

Due to the reasons mentioned above, we see that it is no longer
sensible to continue running the lists in their current state. The
reorganisation evidently needed would take too much of our work time.


The mail volume of the lists has also fallen a lot during the last
year because most of the sensible conversation has moved to similar
but properly administrated lists at vger.rutgers.edu. If you don't
know about these alternative lists, see Linux FAQ question 2.8. It
is available at URL:

  http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/users/iwj10/linux-faq/section2.html


Comments regarding this course of action should be sent to the
address linux-activists-shutdown@niksula.hut.fi, although we may
be unable to answer all replies.

This message has been sent to all current subscribers of
linux-activists@niksula.hut.fi and to comp.os.linux.announce and
comp.os.linux.misc newsgroups.


